course: dictionary
lesson: 207
title: Alcoholic and non-alcoholic
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alcoholic is an adjective when it describes a drink. An alcoholic drink has alcohol in it, like beer, wine or whisky. Non-alcoholic means without alcohol, like juice or lemonade. The little word non- means not, so you can work out the meaning from the parts you already know.
explain: As a noun, an alcoholic is a person who has an illness. The illness makes them need to drink alcohol, and they find it very hard to stop. «Has a drinking problem» means the same thing. It is an illness, and it can hurt the person and the people who love them.
explain: Read the words around the word to find clues. «Refreshments» on an invitation can politely mean alcoholic drinks, so you need to think about the whole sentence. «I'll just have the one» is a well-known joke, because one drink so often becomes three. Children must never drink alcoholic drinks, and nobody should drive after drinking alcohol.
fact: An alcoholic drink has alcohol in it, like beer, wine or whisky.
fact: Non-alcoholic means without alcohol, like juice or lemonade.
fact: «Recovering alcoholic» means a person who is getting better from the illness of needing to drink alcohol.
fact: «One for the road» means one last alcoholic drink before leaving.
fact: A «nightcap» is an alcoholic drink before bed.
exercise: «Has a drinking problem» means a person is an alcoholic. What is an alcoholic? | A person who only drinks juice | *A person who has an illness that makes them need to drink alcohol and find it very hard to stop | A person who has lots of friends | A person who has a sore head after a game
exercise: Which drink is non-alcoholic? | Whisky | Wine | *Lemonade | Beer
exercise: Dad says, «I'll just have the one.» Why is this said as a joke? | *Because one drink so often becomes three | Because it is a kind of cake | Because it means he is very tall | Because it means he will be singing
test: Which word means without alcohol, like juice or lemonade? | Nightcap | Alcoholic | *Non-alcoholic | Refreshments
test: What is a «nightcap»? | A glass of milk | *An alcoholic drink before bed | A warm bath before bed | A bedtime story
exam: Why must children never drink alcoholic drinks? | Because alcoholic drinks are always cold | Because alcoholic drinks taste bad | Because juice is alcoholic | *Because alcohol can harm a growing body
